# Cloudflare Pages Redirects
# This file is intentionally left without wildcard rules to prevent SPA fallback.
# Existing files will be served automatically.
# Non-existent paths will result in a 404 status.
#
# NOTE: Pages Functions run BEFORE this file, and functions/_middleware.js now
# mirrors every path rule below in its RETIRED map so that query-string and
# .html variants resolve in a single hop. These rules therefore act as the
# fallback if a Functions deploy ever fails. Keep the two lists in sync when
# adding or removing a retired path.
#
# Only RETIRED paths need mirroring here. The middleware's other two
# normalizations — collapsing duplicate slashes and stripping `.html` — are
# behaviours Pages already provides natively (it resolves `//` and 308s
# `X.html` → `X`), so if Functions ever fail to deploy those URLs still
# resolve; they just cost a 308 instead of the 301 the middleware returns.

# www -> apex (requires DNS CNAME for www to be configured in Cloudflare)
https://www.simplememofast.com/*  https://simplememofast.com/:splat  301

